think Drew the three light diagonals on the shared 5x7 body: U+2571 the forward slash (upper-right to lower-left), U+2572 the backslash (upper-left to lower-right), U+2573 their cross -- the pen stepping one cell down each row corner to corner, the ASCII art the specification.
think Added one property the straight-line box corpora could not: the cross is EXACTLY the two single diagonals overlaid -- a cell inks in the cross iff either single diagonal inks it (a union) -- which proves the three are a family, not three lone drawings.
obs GREEN on the first build: 3 marks round-trip byte-identical, all present, distinct, legible (ink 7..13 of 35), the union holds, encoded 160 over raw 105 (compression reported, not asserted -- the round-trip is the proof, honoring REDS #82's no-false-invariant rule since the sparse diagonals pay run overhead).
obs Caught and removed a nonsense `c += 0` filler line before the witness ran; the union loop body is a single if.
